\section{Conclusion}
\label{sec:conclusion}

\looseness=-1
Across six benchmarks, 17.9--31.3\% of items exhibit temporal DIF while aggregate rankings remain stable ($\rho \geq 0.994$); base-vs-instruct reversals and web-overlap independence confirm structured signal beyond contamination. Cross-subject matching ($\Delta\mathrm{FPR} = 0$) and DEFF correction provide methodological safeguards against false positives under model-family non-independence. The Monitor/Triage/Correct protocol offers benchmark maintainers empirically grounded thresholds for ongoing psychometric audits.

